# Logitech PRO X2 SUPERSTRIKE (046d:40bd through its 046d:c54d receiver,
# 046d:c0a8 cabled) -> uaccess on its own hidraw node through the receiver,
# and on its HID++ interface, 02, on its cable.
#
# Not yet checked on this hardware. It pairs to the PRO X SUPERLIGHT 2's
# receiver (Solaar issue 3202's listing), so its rules are that mouse's in
# 70-pro-x-superlight-2.rules, for the same reasons: its own node, matched by
# its HID device name, and the c54d pairs two devices, so pair nothing else to
# this mouse's receiver. Cabled, interface 02 is assumed: no source gives its
# cable's interfaces. Interface 01 is not granted.
#
# The node also carries the keystrokes the mouse sends for a button its
# onboard profile binds to a key, as 70-g502x.rules says of the G502 X PLUS's.
#
# No event node is granted: in host mode Gearbench reads its back and forward
# through HID++ on the hidraw nodes below.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0003:046D:40BD.*", TAG+="uaccess"
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="046d", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="c0a8", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"
